-- title:
--   Degree of the base-changed X₀(N) q-expansion field over K(j)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure (so of characteristic $0$), and let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$. Let $F_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$, taken over all weights $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma_0(N)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and all integral power series $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ that are integral $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ respectively, subject to $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g \neq 0$. Let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange K F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) be the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to K((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to K$. Let $y \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K[[q]]$ of the integral power series $E_4^3 \cdot \mathrm{dedekindEtaUnitInv}$. Then the $K\langle y\rangle$-vector space $F$ has finite rank equal to the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_0(N)$ together with the powers of $-I$, where $K\langle y\rangle$ denotes the intermediate field of $F$ generated over $K$ by $y$.
--
--   This is the classical computation of the degree of the function field of $X_0(N)$ over $K(j)$: since $-I \in \Gamma_0(N)$, the join on the right is $\Gamma_0(N)$ itself, and its index is $\psi(N)$. The statement is kept in the shape involving the join with $\langle -I\rangle$ so that it can be used interchangeably with its $\Gamma_1$ counterpart; it feeds the full-level statements bounding relative ranks of adjoined $q$-expansion images.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_adjoin_jqModC_laurentBaseChange_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_eq_index.lean

